<title>GERMANY: Hoechst says no capital rise for U.S. listing.</title>
<headline>Hoechst says no capital rise for U.S. listing.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals and drugs group Hoechst AG said on Wednesday that it would list its shares in New York in October but that it did not plan a capital increase.</p>
<p>&quot;We are currently examining various options to attract the highest possible interest from American investors for the listing in October,&quot; chief financial officer Klaus-Juergen Schmieder said.</p>
<p>&quot;A capital increase is not among them,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Schmieder's comments were issued in a press release.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
